{"evt":"snapshot_stored","id":"d08e0c33-36f1-49a6-b946-dff7dff71c5c/8","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","subject":"daemon: native task lifecycle pipeline (embed + blockedBy wires + judge seed on ingestion)","description":"Implement the core lifecycle function the daemon runs whenever it discovers new/changed native task files. The function takes a task key + file contents and:\n1. Embeds the task (title + description → vec via existing embed() — ~5ms warm, already done for overlay tasks)\n2. Parses blockedBy field → emits blocking edges into overlay (e.g. blockedBy:[\"3\"] → add blocking edge from <session>/3 to this task)\n3. Runs suggest_links on the task → seeds candidate context edges into /judge/next queue at weight 0 (judged:false)\n4. Does NOT auto-wire suggest_links suggest_kind:\"blocking\" as hard blockers — those go into judge queue as context candidates only\n\nThis is the same pipeline overlay/followup tasks already go through. Native tasks currently bypass it (they arrive in buildGraph with no vec, no edges, no judge candidates). The function should be idempotent — safe to call on re-reads of already-processed tasks (skip if vec already set + edges already seeded).\n\nHook into: (a) the fs.watch callback at daemon.js line 184 as a passive fallback, and (b) the /sync/tasks endpoint (separate task) as the synchronous path.","status":"completed","blockedBy":[],"owner":null,"metadata":null,"snapshotted_at":"2026-06-15T02:29:34.298Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-15T02:29:34.424Z"}
